WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:10.570
&gt;&gt;Malcolm Grant: Good morning, and welcome
to this meeting of NHS England here in London.

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:15.600
We are meeting, as we always do, in public.
It is not a public meeting, but we have a

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:22.060
number of important items to discharge this
morning. Just by way of explanation, the Board

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:28.210
meets in public and then we take some business
in private meeting; so-called reserve business,

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:34.970
which by virtue of its confidentiality, cannot
be taken in public. We also work quite commonly

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:38.470
in what we call development sessions, working
on strategy.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:44.590
We spent a great deal of time yesterday thinking
through, both as executive directors and as

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:50.080
non-executive directors, our future strategy
around critical items in the Five-Year Forward

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:56.340
View. The meeting of the Board in public is
both to discharge formal business and also

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:04.360
to symbolise the importance that we attach
to transparency in what we do. A special welcome

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:08.360
to those members of the public who have joined
us here in London this morning.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.000
I declare the meeting formally open

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:21.240
and give advice to everybody that there is no fire alarm scheduled and should it go off then our staff will take

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.540
people to a safe place, off the premises.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:27.860
May I invite any declarations of interest in any matters

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:32.700
on the agenda from members of the Board, other
than those already recorded in the public

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.430
register. No?

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:43.490
I welcome to the Board this morning Richard
Barker, who is acting as National Director

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:51.760
for Commissioning in interim succession to
Barbara Hakin, leading up to the arrival in

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:56.940
May of Matthew Swindells. Richard, thank you
very much for taking on this responsibility

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:01.799
and for joining us this morning. Richard's
other task is as our regional director for

00:02:01.799 --> 00:02:04.210
the North region.

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:10.580
I need to present apologies for Jane Cummings,
who, for family reasons, is not able to be

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:17.209
with us today, and introduce Neil Churchill,
who will speak to us today on the item on

00:02:17.209 --> 00:02:23.340
whistle blowing. At the same time, I introduce
Cally Palmer, who will join us for the item

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:26.430
on the Cancer Taskforce.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:32.400
Just one matter of preliminary business on
behalf of the Chair, which is to inform the

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:40.040
Board formally of the appointment of Moira
Gibb to our Remuneration and Strategic Human

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:46.450
Resources Committee. Thank you, Moira, for
agreeing to take that on. Also, David Roberts

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:51.959
has been appointed as Deputy Chairman of the
Board of NHS England. To the extent that it

00:02:51.959 --> 00:02:56.459
requires the endorsement of the Board, may
I assume that it is enthusiastically given

00:02:56.459 --> 00:03:01.719
to both of those proposals? Good. Thank you
very much indeed.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:08.680
I have not had any comments on the minutes
of the last meeting, so may I take them as

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:13.069
a fair and accurate record? I have not had
any matters arising from them. Does anybody

00:03:13.069 --> 00:03:16.150
have any matters arising? No. Thank you very
much.

